{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/503943-lunars-who-ride","id":503943,"title":"Lunars who ride","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-05T01:47:49-07:00","id":503943,"title":"Lunars who ride","content":"What is a Marukani master horseman supposed to do when Luna Exalts him?<br /> <br /> Supposing that his totem is, quite reasonably, a horse, his riding and mounted archery skills are useless in his spirit shape (or in any other animal form).<br /> <br /> If he uses Deadly Beastman Transformation, his horse is now burdened by a much larger, heavier rider. Also, it's a horse riding a horse. Horseption.<br /> <br /> <br /> For cases like this, it might be cool if a Lunar could temporarily lock out his shapeshifting ability by splitting his spirit shape off to act as a familiar. So he can ride his own bestial soul into battle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T01:52:36-07:00","id":503968,"title":"","content":"In 3rd edition, supposedly DBT is an option, not a necessity. So he could just stay in human form, ride his horse around and have Evocations from his cool Moonsilver bow. <br /> <br /> As another possibility, what about the idea of &quot;melding&quot; Charms, where perhaps the Lunar physically merges with his own horse (turning into something like a Centaur)? That might be kind of an interesting direction to go as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T02:10:33-07:00","id":503998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supposing that his totem is, quite reasonably, a horse, his riding and mounted archery skills are useless in his spirit shape (or in any other animal form).</div> </div> </div> </div> It would seem to me that noticing how the spirit shape invalidates a large portion of the character concept makes it eminently <i>un</i>reasonable for it to be that shape. You can have an equestrian culture without having everybody literally have the spirit of a horse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T05:46:23-07:00","id":504070,"title":"","content":"I recall the idea of Lunars having some pretty good Familiar Charms being forwarded, even if they don't exactly have ones to ride. I can see at least one application of that being able to make a mount accommodate a notably increased mass.<br /> <br /> Merging with a horse to become a centaur just feels... weird to me. Although I find it crass in myself, it keeps making it feel like a human centipede kind of situation.<br /> <br /> Although for Infernals...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T07:40:09-07:00","id":504129,"title":"","content":"What if a horse-totem Lunar could have their DBT form be a centaur? Maybe make DBT more flexible so it isn't always anthropomorphic beastfolk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T08:35:06-07:00","id":504185,"title":"","content":"Speaking purely for myself, I would be amenable to thinking of a horse-based war form that is still quadrupedal, while still not having the whole &quot;human torso at the top/end of an animal&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> I mean, barring some very interesting carvings taken from the Parthenon*, centaurs and their derivatives just look distractingly goofy to me. And the idea of a person shapeshifting into one... it would strike me as less &quot;impressive and fearsome transformation into battle form&quot; and more &quot;regular person who grows a horse out of their behind&quot;.<br /> <br /> I mean, with some exceptions; a serpentine body feels like a more organic transition to me, because it's a lot less busy and skewed, and follows the lines suggestive of legs that have blended together.<br /> <br /> I mean, the asymmetry of a centaur alone...<br /> <br /> * And that's mostly for the sake of my admiration for how much thought and creativity the sculptors obviously put in to imagining what a centaur might look like in a battle, how its muscles might have connected and contorted in the course of such exertions, as well as the attention to detail in how the still poses look like the transitions in dynamic and realistic fighting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T09:07:51-07:00","id":504232,"title":"","content":"Turning into a small animal and using Ride to drive humans around as mounts after leaping onto them, perhaps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T09:23:04-07:00","id":504281,"title":"","content":"Take a look at this picture:<br /> <img src=\"http://www.nps.gov/parkhistory/online_books/kcc/images/fig8-4.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> See the guy on the right who's practically falling out of that saddle in order to get an angle for a shot underneath his target's defence?<br /> <br /> While an animal form might not necessarily wield a bow, I could say a horse rider having a form with some particulars of size and flexibility and grip that would let them use their horse as a mobile platform from which to launch attacks at multiple angles, many of which a human on a horse isn't really built to defend against.<br /> <br /> Or they can combine rapid form shifting with archery with a horse to be able to get in the air, launch strikes and land on something that will let them preserve momentum.<br /> <br /> Now I've also got an idea of a Lunar who turns into a ferret or something who brings their horse up close to that of an enemy and runs down the saddle along the underbelly of their mount and across to the other one to bite at the stomach or the gonads or the legs in order to cause that horse to disastrously trip over or veer off while rapidly scurrying back over to their own.<br /> <br /> Then shifting back to a human and letting off a parting shot at the possibly still alive rider for good measure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T09:24:08-07:00","id":504283,"title":"","content":"Just gonna drop in my contractually obligated blob of EX3 What We Know stuff. It makes up most of the <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Charms#Lunar_Charms\" target=\"_blank\">Lunar Charms subsection</a>, at the moment.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EX3 What We Know Wiki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Q: (ChrisARose)</b><br /> Will Lunar's have anything like a ride charm or a beast-master charm - or is this not really a focus for Lunars?<br /> <br /> <b>A: (John M\u00f8rke)</b><br /> Taming Charms? I can dig it.<br /> Riding Charms? Only if you can come up with awesome mounted Lunar ideas.<br /> <br /> <b>Q: (ChrisARose)</b><br /> So like a No-Moon with something like Sleipnir - a blazing pineal eye swirling with the spark of the Wyld within - showing paths unseen. They plod past war torn fields, a living soul never gracing their presence. Following not land mark or star - but the undulating song of what is to come - the after images of dreams so vivid they have subsumed reality.<br /> <br /> A Full-Moon with a demonic beast that shifts and changes. Even as a sword pierces its hide, a pulse of flesh, and a chitinous plate erupts to the surface forcing the blade away. Awakening the spark of Chthonic Baara is dangerous, it can never be coaxed to sleep again, always hungry and ever changing. It is troublesome finding new beings for it to consume - to sate its need to bring all the scattered parts of itself back together...one beast at a time.<br /> <br /> Or the Changing Moon who's never truly alone. The voices howl and coo in her head even as the moonsilver tattoos show those outside a stable form. A thought, a break in the skin, and they can come rushing out - a Kirin to bear her away from a timber fire or some lesser beast to give warm and comfort on a cold stormy night. Sometimes she visits them in her dreams - for they are of her blood.<br /> <br /> When I hunt, Strig is always at my side. Luna watches us, stalking the prey by her light alone. I can feel its heart beating - the heat rising from it body. It is over quickly - ritual is a clean thing. I bite down upon the leathery heart and look up to my brother...he's already cracked the skull like a nut and devoured the meat within. Even as the blood of the hunted now courses in my veins - the light in his eyes shows that the memories of the slain live on.<br /> <br /> Or am I way off base on what your talking about here?<br /> <br /> <b>A: (John M\u00f8rke)</b><br /> You're not off-base. This is closer to what I was looking for than any other idea I've seen. I mean, Lunars riding horses and tigers, sure. But I wouldn't give them ride-enhancing Charms for that, because those are off-beats. They don't really fit the iconography, since Lunars can become animals. So I am more compelled by ideas that proceed from the basis of Lunars who ride creatures that compliment them.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EX3 What We Know Wiki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Q: (Matt the Bruins fan)</b><br /> Razzin' frazzin' Solars... I guess this means my Lunar needs to get cracking on his plan to make off into the Wyld with a viable breeding population of chameleons and start selecting for gigantism. Let's see your golden camo dinosaurs climb redwoods, spot opponents over a 360\u00b0 arc, and use their tongues as ballistic seige weapons!<br /> <br /> <b>A: (The Demented One) </b><br /> I don't think Lunars will be disappointed with their familiars. Not if I have any Charms to write about it.</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T10:00:03-07:00","id":504342,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/VTZGcTL.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> That is all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T10:04:23-07:00","id":504344,"title":"","content":"Bears riding sharks.<br /> <br /> Yes, on land.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T10:10:32-07:00","id":504352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/503943-lunars-who-ride?p=504342#post504342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jeez, I feel as though just looking at this picture will poke my eyes out. <br /> <br /> I'm going to employ the shades-smiley, but only to have a protective covering of my vit